\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The two-point average}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Let #{2} be a unit in the commutative ring #{k}, and let #{A=k\times k} with pointwise product. The constant pairs #{B=\{(c,c):c\in k\}} form a unital subalgebra. The swap of the two coordinates is a unital automorphism, and
##{E(a,b)=\left(\frac{a+b}2,\frac{a+b}2\right)}
is a [normalized conditional functional](fdip-00KV) of #{A} onto #{B}. It is the average of the identity and the swap. On a constant pair it is the identity, and a constant factor pulls out of both coordinates.}
